**B. Task model and frontmatter persistence**

- **`task.Task` fields** (`internal/task/task.go:46-92`):
  - `ID`, `ParentID` (omitempty), `Title`, `Description` (`yaml:"-"`, it is the body), `Status`, `Priority`, `Type`, `Relations` (omitempty);
  - `CreatedAt` and `UpdatedAt` (`time.Time`, **not** omitempty, `:56-57`);
  - `Resolution`, `ResolutionNote`, `ClosedAt *time.Time`, `VerifiedAt *time.Time`, all omitempty (`:63-75`);
  - the branch fields `Branch`, `BaseBranch`, `StartCommit`, `FinalBranch`, `SquashCommit`, all omitempty (`:77-91`).
  - No field records a creator, and no field records anything about phases.
- **Writing.** `MarkdownStorage.Save` does not encode `task.Task` directly. It builds an anonymous frontmatter struct that lists every key, so a new key must be added there explicitly (`internal/storage/markdown.go:45-85`).
  - Optional keys use `omitempty`. Optional timestamps are rendered as `""` through `formatTime` so the key disappears (`:57-65, 241-248`).
  - `created_at` and `updated_at` are always written, in `2006-01-02T15:04:05Z07:00` format (`:74-75`).
  - YAML key order follows the struct field order. The write is atomic (`writeFileAtomic`: write `<path>.tmp`, then rename, after `MkdirAll` of the parent; `:97, 100-111`).
- **Reading.** `parse` decodes into a second hand-written struct with `yaml.Unmarshal`. That call is not strict (`KnownFields` is never enabled), so unknown keys are ignored and missing keys load as zero values (`markdown.go:181-203`).
  - Timestamps are parsed with errors ignored (`:215-216`). Optional ones go through `parseOptionalTime`, where empty or unparsable reads as nil (`:250-262`).
  - Every field must also be copied into the returned `Task` by hand (`:218-238`).
- **Precedent for adding fields.** `_design.md` records it: "All four keys are `omitempty`: an open task's frontmatter is byte-identical … and old files parse unchanged. No migration runs" (`_design.md:137-139`). The storage test `TestMarkdownStorage_ResolutionRoundTrip` checks the round trip and checks that empty keys are not emitted (`internal/storage/storage_test.go:2537-2611`).
- **The in-memory index is a projection.** `IndexEntry` (`internal/storage/index.go:27-52`) carries:
  - `ID`, `ParentID`, `Title`, `Status`, `Priority`, `Type`, `CreatedAt`, `UpdatedAt`;
  - `Resolution`, `ClosedAt`, `VerifiedAt`;
  - `Branch`, `FinalBranch`, `SquashCommit`.

  `Description`, `ResolutionNote`, `BaseBranch` and `StartCommit` are left out on purpose. `taskToEntry` and `entryToTask` copy these fields by hand (`:54-96`).
  - **Who reads only index fields:** `Index.All`, `Filter`, `GetSubtasks` and `NextTodo` return index-only tasks (`internal/task/service.go:49-53`; `index.go:285-337`). That includes `list_tasks`, CLI `list`, and every card on the board (`BoardSnapshot.Tasks`, `internal/task/view.go:24-26, 60`). A field missing from `IndexEntry` is therefore missing from all of those outputs.
  - **Self-healing** compares only `{id}/{id}.md` mtimes and the task count (`index.go:206-245`, the stat at `:224`). Attached files never mark the index stale.
- **Scans.** `LoadAll` and `isStaleOnDisk` skip non-directories, `archive` and `.users` (`markdown.go:141`; `index.go:220`).

**C. Create path**

- **MCP.** `create_task` → `createTaskHandler` reads `title`, `description`, `priority`, `type`, `parent_id` and `id`, then calls `svc.Create(title, description, priority, taskType, parentID, customID)` and returns `taskResult(t)`, which is the whole `task.Task` marshalled as JSON (`internal/tools/management.go:154-170, 413-419`).
- **Service.** `Service.Create` locks and calls `create` (`internal/task/service.go:202-206`). `create` does the following, in order:
  1. validates title, priority and type;
  2. validates the parent: it must exist and must not itself be a subtask;
  3. runs `EnsureDir`;
  4. validates a custom id, or allocates `index.NextID()`;
  5. stamps `now := time.Now().UTC()` into **both** `CreatedAt` and `UpdatedAt`, with status `todo` (`:251-262`);
  6. runs `storage.Save` and then `index.Set` (`:208-271`).

  `create` takes no identity parameter and stamps nothing about the user. `CreateSubtask` is a second exported entry point into the same twin (`:274-278`).
- **Who calls `Create`:**
  - in production, `internal/tools/management.go:163` and `internal/cli/commands.go:256`;
  - in test support, `internal/testsupport/testsupport.go:76` (`Seed`);
  - in tests, 12 `_test.go` files.
- **CLI.** `mcp-task-manager create <title> [-p] [-t] [-d] [--parent] [--id] [--json]` (`internal/cli/cli.go:91-106`) → `cmdCreate` → `svc.Create`. It prints `FormatTaskDetail(t)`, or the task as JSON (`internal/cli/commands.go:249-273`).

**D. User identity**

- **Resolution.** `vcs.ResolveIdentity(root)` runs `git config --get user.email` (works outside a repository). It keeps only the part before `@` and sanitizes it (`internal/vcs/vcs.go:317-334`).
  - Sanitizing (`:358-383`): lowercase; runes outside `[a-z0-9._-]` become `-`; runs of `-` collapse; leading and trailing `.`/`-` are trimmed; `..` becomes `.`; a trailing `.lock` is stripped.
  - **Fallback order:** `user.Current().Username` (the part after `\`), then `$USER`, then `$USERNAME`, then `"default"`, with `FromGitEmail: false` (`:336-350`).
  - **The full email is never kept.** `vcs.Identity` has only `Name` and `FromGitEmail` (`:43-49`).
- **Injection.** `task.Identity{Name, FromGitEmail}` is set with `WithIdentity` (`internal/task/git.go:37-43, 61-64`) and stored in the write-once field `Service.identity` (`service.go:107-113`).
- **Construction.** `project.Build` is the single construction site. It **always** resolves the identity and passes `WithCurrentTaskStore(mdStorage)` and `WithIdentity(...)`, whatever `cfg.Git.Branching` says. `WithGit(vcs.New(root, tasksDir))` is added only when branching is on (`internal/project/resolver.go:131-166`, lines `150-157`). So an identity is available with branching off too. It costs one `git config` process per Build.
- **What the identity is used for today:**
  - branch names (`wipBranch(s.identity.Name, …)`, `branching_start.go:104`);
  - the pointer user (`current.go:25, 47, 50, 60-73`);
  - the branching precondition `FromGitEmail` (`branching_start.go:38-40`, `errNoEmail` at `:20`).
- **No exported accessor.** No exported `Service` method returns the identity. `keepsPointer()` is false when `identity.Name == ""` (`current.go:38-40`).
- **Test identities:**

  | Test service | Identity |
  |---|---|
  | `testsupport.NewBacklog` | `Identity{Name: "dev"}`, not from git email (`internal/testsupport/testsupport.go:35-36`) |
  | `NewGitBacklog` | `dev`, resolved from repository email `dev@example.com` (`internal/testsupport/gitbacklog.go:53-56`; `git.go:58-60`) |
  | In-package `newConcurrentService` | none (`internal/task/concurrency_test.go:17-26`) |
  | In-package `newPointerService` | `dev` (`internal/task/current_test.go:38-44`) |

- **In this repository** the identity is `igor.cwer`: the pointer directory and the branch prefix show it.

**E. Attached files**

- **Validation.** `validatePathSegment` rejects empty or blank names, names with `/` or `\`, and `..` (`internal/storage/files.go:14-25`). `validateFilename` adds one reserved name, the task's own `{id}.md`, and only when writing (`:32-40`).
  - **No other names are reserved, and no suffixes are restricted.** `research.phase` is a valid attached filename today.
  - Reserved task **ids** are a separate map: `"0"`, `"archive"`, `".index.json"`, `.users` (`:44-49`).
- **Write.** `MarkdownStorage.WriteFile` validates, then writes atomically into `tasks/{id}/` (`files.go:71-78`). The storage layer does not check that the task exists; `writeFileAtomic` would `MkdirAll`. The service does check, in `Service.WriteTaskFile`: the task must be in the active index, an archived task is refused with "task %s is archived; files are read-only", and anything else is "task not found" (`service.go:318-331`).
- **Read and list.** `ReadFile` and `ListFiles` resolve the directory as active first, then archive (`files.go:80-101, 103-125, 127-138`).
  - `ListFiles` drops subdirectories and `{id}.md`, and returns every other entry in `os.ReadDir` order, which is sorted by filename (`:111-124`).
  - It does not filter `*.tmp` leftovers or dotfiles.
  - The in-package `mockFileStorage.ListFiles` returns map order, i.e. unsorted (`internal/task/service_test.go:141-147`).
- **Service methods without twins.** `WriteTaskFile`, `ReadTaskFile` and `ListTaskFiles` take the lock and do the work inline (`service.go:320-355`). Code that already holds `s.mu` must call `s.fileStorage` directly.
- **Interface.** `task.FileStorage` has just `WriteFile`, `ReadFile` and `ListFiles` (`service.go:87-96`). `NewService` receives the same `*MarkdownStorage` as `Storage`, `ArchiveStorage`, `FileStorage` and the pointer store (`resolver.go:160`).
- **Read-only consumers.** `Service.attachedFiles(id)` is an unlocked helper: a nil file store, or a listing error, reads as "no files" (`internal/task/view.go:92-105`). `detail()` puts the result in `TaskDetail.Files` for active and archived tasks (`view.go:115-139`).
- **Tools.** `write_task_file` takes `task_id`, `filename` and `content`, all required. `read_task_file` and `list_task_files` call `EnsureProjectExists` first. `list_task_files` returns a JSON array, or the text "No files attached to task X" (`internal/tools/files.go:14-120`). The descriptions are minimal (`internal/tools/descriptions/write_task_file.yaml:1-5`, `list_task_files.yaml:1-3`).
- **CLI.** `write-task-file`, `read-task-file` and `list-task-files` exist (`internal/cli/commands.go:415-468`).

**F. How the phase is derived today**

- **Type.** `task.Phase` has the constants `research`, `design`, `planning` and `implementation`. `Phases()` returns them in workflow order. `Order()` maps anything unknown to 0 (`internal/task/phase.go:8-35`).
- **Mapping.** `phaseMarkers` maps file names to the phase a task has *reached* (`phase.go:37-48`):

  | Attached file | Phase |
  |---|---|
  | `task` | research |
  | `research` | design |
  | `design` | planning |
  | `plan` | implementation |
  | `implementation` | implementation |

  `phaseFromFiles` lowercases each name and trims one `.md`, matches exactly, takes the maximum rank, and defaults to Research (`:50-62`). A name such as `research.phase` matches no marker and is ignored; near-miss tests such as `plan.txt` and `plan.tmp` show this (`internal/task/phase_test.go:38-47`).
- **Snapshot.** `boardSnapshot()` runs under the one lock. It takes `index.All()` and, **for in-progress tasks only**, sets `snap.Phases[id] = phaseFromFiles(s.attachedFiles(id))`. That is one directory listing per in-progress task per snapshot, and no file contents are read (`view.go:59-90`, lines `73-75`). `BoardSnapshot.Phases` documents that a missing entry reads as Research (`view.go:33-36`).
- **Grouping.** The "furthest phase of the group" rule lives in the web view model. `newPhaseLanes` gives each root In-progress card the maximum `Order()` over itself and its nested subtasks; a lane's `Count` is 1 plus the number of nested subtasks (`internal/web/view.go:215-234`). A subtask shown standalone uses its own phase.
- **Failure fallback.** No file store, or a failed listing, reads as Research (`internal/task/view_test.go:131-173`). CLAUDE.md documents the whole rule (`CLAUDE.md:237`).
- **Earlier decisions.** The in-progress-phase-columns task decided "No new frontmatter field, no tool/schema changes; purely read-side" (`tasks/in-progress-phase-columns/task:9`). Its design listed as non-goals: a phase chip on cards, and phases in the detail view, CLI or MCP tools (`tasks/in-progress-phase-columns/design:39-45, 330-332`).

**G. Lifecycle: `start_task`, `complete_task`, `update_task`**

*Handlers*

- **`start_task`** handler: `svc.StartTask(id)`, result `taskResult(t)` (`internal/tools/workflow.go:95-106`).
- **`complete_task`** handler: builds `WithResolution` and `WithResolutionNote` only when the key is present, `WithCommitMessage` when the value is non-empty, then calls `svc.CompleteTask` followed by `svc.RunAutoArchive()` (error ignored) (`workflow.go:108-134`).
- **`update_task`** handler: builds pointer arguments only for keys that are present, plus the resolution, note and `verified` options, then calls `svc.Update` (`management.go:253-301`).

*`StartTask` → `startTask`* (`service.go:616-650`)

1. Load the task with `get`, which falls back to the archive.
2. **Restart check.** If `s.git != nil`, `t.Branch != ""`, the status is `todo` or `in_progress`, and the wip ref exists (`git.BranchSHA`), it calls `restartBranched(t)` (`:629-636`).
3. Otherwise the status must be `todo`, or the call fails with "task %s is not in todo status (current: %s)" (`:638-640`). So an `in_progress` task **without** a branch, or whose branch ref is gone, cannot be started again.
4. The `blockedError` check (`:642-644`; defined at `branching_restart.go:108-119`).
5. With git: `startBranched` (`:646-648`). Without: `startPlain` (`:649`).

*The start flows*

- **`startPlain`** journals only records and the pointer. It calls `startTaskRecords`, which auto-starts a `todo` parent and then the task itself through `updateStatus`, then `setPointer`. Everything runs inside `runFlow` with a `gitTxn` (`service.go:652-682`).
- **`startBranched`** sends a subtask to `startSub` and a top-level task to `startFresh` (`branching_start.go:251-258`).
- **`startFresh`** (design 5.2), in order (`branching_start.go:262-292`):
  1. `preflightGit`: `git.Check`, `identity.FromGitEmail` (else `errNoEmail`), `Head` (a detached HEAD is refused) and `IndexTree` (`:34-50`).
  2. `planFresh`: `FirstExistingBranch(cfg.Git.BaseBranches)`; wip = `<user>/wip/<shortName>`; final derived from wip; `BranchAvailable(wip)`; the final branch must be free or equal `t.FinalBranch` (`:99-123`).
  3. `classifyVacate(h, carryFrom=plan.base, self="", …)` (`:145-167`).
     - Clean: nothing to do.
     - HEAD is the `Branch` of an `in_progress` task: checkpoint on it (`wipOwner`, `:127-137`).
     - HEAD is the chosen base: changes are carried.
     - Anything else: refused with "uncommitted changes on X (…up to 20 paths); commit or stash them before starting <id>".
     - `DirtyPaths` excludes the tasks directory.
  4. Inside `runFlow`: `checkpoint` (a `Snapshot` commit, journaled), then `startOnNewBranch`, then `switchTo(wip)` (the only worktree change), then `afterSwitch`, which runs `index.Load()`.
- **`startOnNewBranch`** (`:294-313`) is reused for a todo parent. It runs:
  1. `createBranch(wip, tip)`, journaled by `DeleteBranch`;
  2. `updateStatus(t → in_progress, withBranch{Branch, BaseBranch, StartCommit})`, with the record journaled by `captureTask`;
  3. `setPointer`, journaled.

  **None of these checks the task's current status.** Status preconditions live in `startTask`.
- **`startSub`** (`:315-374`):
  - If the parent is `in_progress` and has **no** branch, the subtask is started with `startPlain`: record-only, no git, even while branching is on (`:324-326`).
  - Otherwise it runs `preflightGit`, then `parentLineFor` (`branching_restart.go:164-220`):
    - a `done` parent is refused;
    - an `in_progress` parent must have a live wip;
    - a `todo` parent is restarted in place if its branch ref exists, otherwise **started fresh with its own wip branch inside the same journal** (`planFresh` + `startOnNewBranch(p…)`, `:210-219`).
  - Then: sub-wip `<parent wip>--<shortName>`, `BranchAvailable`, vacate, `startOnNewBranch(t, subWip, parentBranch, ptip)`, switch to the sub-wip.
- **Restart, `restartBranched`** (design 5.4; `branching_restart.go:14-106`):
  1. The blocked check, only for `todo` (`:20-24`).
  2. `preflightGit`, then `wipTip`, which checks that `StartCommit` resolves and is an ancestor of the wip tip (`:121-149`).
  3. Pick the target: a top-level task uses `baseFor(t)` (`BaseBranch` if it still exists, else the first base, `branching_start.go:74-85`); a subtask uses the parent line.
  4. `classifyVacate(h, "", self=t.ID, …)`.
  5. In the flow: checkpoint, an optional parent step, then `restartRecords`. That `git.Replay`s the wip onto the target tip if it moved, refusing on conflicts, moves the ref by compare-and-swap unless it is checked out, and runs `updateStatus(→ in_progress, BaseBranch/StartCommit rewritten)` (`:235-264`).
  6. `setPointer`, then either `switchTo(t.Branch)` or `ResetKeep(newTip)` when HEAD is already on the wip.

  So `start_task` on an **in_progress** task whose wip ref exists always goes through restart: a rebase if the base moved, then a checkout. It is never a no-op error.

*`CompleteTask` → `completeTask`* (`service.go:704-751`)

1. Already closed: refused.
2. A delivered resolution needs `in_progress`. A non-delivered one may close from `todo`.
3. Open subtasks block a delivered close only.
4. **Git dispatch.** Only `if s.git != nil && t.Branch != ""` (`:741-745`) does it go to `completeBranched`. Otherwise it is record-only through `runFlow(completeRecords)` (`:747-750`).
   - So an `in_progress` task **without** `branch` completes record-only with no git calls, even with branching on. `TestLegacyInProgressTaskNoGitCalls` checks this, asserting zero mutating git calls (`internal/task/branching_complete_test.go:446-466`).

*The completion flows*

- **`completeBranched`** (`branching_complete.go:8-35`):

  | Case | Flow |
  |---|---|
  | Delivered subtask whose parent has a `Branch` | `completeSubDelivered` |
  | Other delivered | `completeDelivered` |
  | Non-delivered, branch checked out | `completeAbandoned` |
  | Non-delivered, branch not checked out | `handled=false`, falls through to record-only |

  A delivered subtask **with** a branch whose parent has **no** branch takes the top-level `completeDelivered` path, and gets a final branch `finalBranch(t.Branch)` (`:13-25`).
- **`completeDelivered`** (design 5.5; `:107-169`):
  - Preflight: `preflightWip` (HEAD must be `t.Branch`; `StartCommit` must be an ancestor of HEAD, `:37-51`), the final-branch ownership check, `subtaskGate` (`:53-78`) and `commitMessageFor`.
  - Flow: `snapshotHead`; `CommitTree(TreeOf(W), StartCommit, msg)`; create the final branch, or move it by compare-and-swap; `completeRecords(..., withBranch{FinalBranch, SquashCommit})`; `switchTo(final)`.
- **`completeSubDelivered`** (design 5.6; `:171-217`): snapshot; `MergeTrees(StartCommit, ptip, W)`, where conflicts fail and roll back; `CommitTree(merged, ptip)`; `moveBranch(p.Branch)`; record with `SquashCommit`; switch to the parent's wip.
- **`completeAbandoned`** (`:219-248`): safety snapshot, then records, then switch to `returnTarget` (the parent's wip, or the base).
- **`completeRecords`** (`:98-105`) = `completeTaskRecords` + `clearPointerIf`. `completeTaskRecords` (`service.go:753-813`):
  - journals and cascades open subtasks through `closeSubtasksWith` (`:815-829`);
  - closes the task;
  - auto-completes the parent when every sibling is done, **unless the parent has a `Branch`** (`:795-804`).

*Journal, guard and update*

- **`gitTxn`.** A slice of named undo closures; `rollback()` runs them in reverse and joins the errors (`internal/task/branching.go:149-182`).
  - Undo kinds that exist today: task records (`captureTask`, `:184-204`), the pointer (`capturePointer`, `:214-232`), branch create, move and snapshot (`branching_start.go:181-218`), and `ResetKeep` inside restart.
  - **No undo kind exists for attached files.**
  - `updateStatus` = `captureTask` + `update` (`branching.go:206-212`). `runFlow` rolls back on error (`branching_start.go:241-249`). `withRollback` joins a rollback error (`service.go:684-692`).
- **Update guard.** `Update` runs `branchingGuard` only when `s.git != nil` (`service.go:412-425`). It refuses three moves (`branching.go:234-251`):
  - `todo → in_progress`: "git branching is enabled; use start_task …";
  - closing an `in_progress` task that has a `Branch`;
  - `done → in_progress` for a task with a `Branch`.

  Reopening to `todo` is allowed. With branching on, `update_task` therefore cannot move a task to `in_progress`.
- **`update`.**
  - Reopening clears `Resolution`, `ResolutionNote` and `ClosedAt` (`service.go:493-502`).
  - Branch fields change only through the unexported `withBranch(branchInfo)`, and survive a reopen (`:504-508`; `branching.go:253-285`).
  - `UpdatedAt` is restamped on every update (`:519`).
- **`UpdateOption`** is the variadic pattern for adding inputs without breaking callers (`service.go:368-410`; `_design.md:155-157`).

*Pointer*

- `setPointer` writes the user's pointer, journaled. `clearPointerIf` moves it to the still-open parent, or removes it, but only when it names a task the call closed (`internal/task/current.go:42-74`).
- `CurrentTask` reads it; `get` includes archived tasks (`current.go:13-34`).
- Storage: `<tasks_dir>/.users/<user>/current_task`, written atomically, where a missing file means no pointer (`internal/storage/current.go:9-59`).
- Start writes the pointer in every path: `startPlain` (`service.go:660`), `startOnNewBranch` (`branching_start.go:309`) and restart (`branching_restart.go:86`).

*Commit messages*

- The default squash message is the title, the description and a `Task: <id>` trailer. Bookkeeping commits use fixed subjects such as `wip(<id>): checkpoint before …` (`branching.go:103-147`).

**H. Tool registration and descriptions**

- **Assembly.** `tools.Build` assembles management, workflow, relation, file and web tools. `Register` calls `s.AddTools` (`internal/tools/tools.go:23-43`). `withService` resolves the project lazily and turns resolution errors into tool errors (`:45-56`).
- **Pattern.** Each tool:
  1. calls `textFor("<name>")`;
  2. builds `mcp.NewTool(name, mcp.WithDescription(...), mcp.WithString/WithBoolean(param, mcp.Required()?, mcp.Description(text.param(param)), mcp.Enum(...)?))`;
  3. appends `server.ServerTool{Tool, Handler}` (e.g. `workflow.go:12-61`, `management.go:15-152`).
- **Description text** comes from embedded `internal/tools/descriptions/*.yaml` (`description:` plus `params:` map) (`descriptions.go:11-50`). A missing YAML file or param entry **panics** (`:52-72`).
