**I. Concurrency discipline**

- **One mutex.** `Service.mu` is the only lock. Exported methods lock and delegate to unexported twins and never call exported methods (`service.go:115-123`; `CLAUDE.md:486-493`).
- **Deliberately unlocked**, because they read write-once fields: `EnsureProjectExists`, `ProjectFound`, `Config`, `BranchingEnabled` (`service.go:142-171`; `view.go:197-202`).
- **`TestServiceNoSelfDeadlock`** (`internal/task/concurrency_test.go:104-152`) calls a **hand-written list** of exported methods on one goroutine under a 10 s watchdog. It does not enumerate methods by reflection, so a new exported method is only checked if it is added to that list. CLAUDE.md says the test "fails if a new method breaks the shape" (`CLAUDE.md:488`); in code that holds only for methods in the list.
- **`TestServiceRace`** runs hand-listed readers and writers concurrently over lock-free in-package mocks. The writers include `StartTask`, `CompleteTask` and `WriteTaskFile` (`concurrency_test.go:56-102`).
- **Web race test.** `TestHandlerRaceAgainstWrites` mixes HTTP GETs with `Create`, `Update` and `WriteTaskFile` on an in-progress task (`internal/web/race_test.go:19-69`, `WriteTaskFile` at `:66`).
- **Git runs under the lock**, and web reads wait for it (`CLAUDE.md:490`).

